Title: The Impact of the New 59Fe Decay Rates on 60Fe and 26Al Nucleosynthesis in Massive Stars
Authors: Tan B., Xin W., Jiang R., Zhao G., and Takahashi K.
Table: Basic evolution properties of the stellar models
================================================================================
Byte-by-byte Description of file: table.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes Format Units  Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1- 2  A2      ---    59Fe_decay_rate Decay rate of 59Fe, DR=Default Rate (LMP,
                                    2001); NR=New Rate (Gao et al., 2021)
 4- 5  I2     solMass M_ini           [14/80] Initial mass of the star
 7-12  F6.3   solMass M_fin           [12.89/38.05] Final mass of the star at
                                    the end of the pre-SN simulation
14-19  F6.3   solMass M_He            [4.19/35.75] Mass of the helium core at
                                    the helium depletion
21-26  F6.3   solMass M_CO            [2.48/31.78] Mass of the carbon-oxygen
                                    core at helium depletion
28-31  F4.2   solMass M_cut           [1.43/2.66] Mass cut before the supernova
                                    explosion
33-37  F5.2   solMass M_fb            Mass of fallback material after the
                                    supernova explosion
39-43  F5.2   solMass M_rem           [1.43/32.35] Mass of the compact remnant
                                    left behind after the supernova explosion
45-49  F5.2   solMass M_ej            [2.29/30.58] Mass of the total material
                                    ejected after the supernova explosion
51-55  F5.3    ---    X(12C)          [0.11/0.29] Mass fraction of carbon-12 of
                                    the center of the star at helium depletion
57-62  F6.3    Myr    tau_H           [3.09/12.86] Lifetime of the star during
                                    the hydrogen burning phase
64-68  F5.3    Myr    tau_He          [0.34/1.46] Lifetime of the star during
                                    the helium burning phase
70-75  F6.3    Myr    tau_total       [3.44/14.35] Total lifetime of the star
                                    from the zero-age main sequence to the end
                                    of the pre-SN simulation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
